  "verbalization": "Fluticasone Propionate, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Fluticasone Propionate may exert its effects on Allergic Rhinitis via the indirect route through Desonide and Prednisone, both of which are corticosteroids with anti-inflammatory properties. The presence of a direct indication from Fluticasone Propionate to Allergic Rhinitis, albeit with lower scores compared to the other paths, indicates a potential role in the condition, though the strength of this link is moderate. The shared pathway involving corticosteroids points to a common mechanism of action, likely involving the suppression of inflammatory responses and immune modulation. The evidence from multiple paths supports the idea that corticosteroids may contribute to the treatment of Allergic Rhinitis, though the exact mechanism and the degree of relevance of Fluticasone Propionate remain to be fully elucidated.",
